Feature: Users Active Count Endpoint
  As a caller of the user service
  I want GET /users/active-count to answer with the number of active users and the number of inactive users as separate counts
  So that I can see both numbers in one request

  Background:
    Given the user service is running

  # Why: The core ask — two numbers, kept apart, from one request.
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Active and inactive users are counted separately
    Given three active users and two inactive users exist
    When a GET request to /users/active-count is sent
    Then the status code should be 200
    And the response body should show an active count of 3 and an inactive count of 2

  # Why: "As separate counts" means two named numbers, never one combined total.
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The reply names its two numbers active and inactive
  @key-example
  Scenario: The two counts are separate fields in the reply
    Given one active user and one inactive user exist
    When a GET request to /users/active-count is sent
    Then the status code should be 200
    And the response body should carry the two numbers under separate names, active and inactive

  # Why: Just-inside boundary — the smallest possible answer is two zeros, not an error.
  @boundary
  Scenario: No users gives zero for both counts
    Given no users exist
    When a GET request to /users/active-count is sent
    Then the status code should be 200
    And the response body should show an active count of 0 and an inactive count of 0

  # Why: Boundary — one side empty, the other side carrying every user.
  @boundary
  Scenario: Only active users gives an inactive count of zero
    Given two active users and no inactive users exist
    When a GET request to /users/active-count is sent
    Then the status code should be 200
    And the response body should show an active count of 2 and an inactive count of 0

  # Why: Boundary — the mirror image, so neither number is silently dropped when it is zero.
  @boundary
  Scenario: Only inactive users gives an active count of zero
    Given two inactive users and no active users exist
    When a GET request to /users/active-count is sent
    Then the status code should be 200
    And the response body should show an active count of 0 and an inactive count of 2

  # Why: The route is read-only; a write to it must be refused, not silently accepted.
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] A POST to /users/active-count is refused with 405
  @negative
  Scenario: Posting to the count route is not allowed
    Given three active users exist
    When a POST request to /users/active-count is sent
    Then the status code should be 405
    And the response body should say the method is not allowed

  # Why: The service offers JSON; a caller asking for another format is told so plainly.
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The count route offers JSON only and refuses other Accept headers with 406
  @negative
  Scenario: Asking for the counts in a format other than JSON is refused
    Given three active users exist
    When a GET request to /users/active-count is sent with an Accept header of text/xml
    Then the status code should be 406
